# Build context hygiene for deploy/Dockerfile (home-base image).
# Persistent/host state never ships in the image — it lives in the
# /app/data volume, created by first-run init (tools/init).
#
# NOTE: .git is intentionally NOT excluded. deploy/Dockerfile stamps /app/VERSION
# from it and KEEPS it: the node's /app (and the autonomy-code volume it seeds) is
# a working checkout that follows origin (tools/dashboard/software_update.py).
# So nothing git TRACKS may be excluded here — a tracked file missing from /app
# reads as a deletion, the tree is dirty, and the update guard (can_update)
# refuses on every node built from the image. Excluded directories re-include
# their tracked files below; deploy/tests/test_dockerignore_keeps_tracked_files.py
# fails if a tracked file is ever excluded again. Only deploy/Dockerfile builds
# from this context; the agent images use their own flat context
# (agents/build.sh).

.venv
.browser_profile
data
!data/uploads/.gitkeep
node_modules
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
.pytest_cache

# Host-local binaries (gitignored anyway; agent images copy these, the
# home-base image does not)
agents/bin
agents/images
!agents/images/dashboard/Dockerfile
tools/dashboard/tailwindcss

# Scratch
*.log
/tmp
